{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",
  "_comment": [
    "Shared, committed agent governance. Every session — local, worktree, cloud,",
    "headless — inherits this file. Machine-local overrides go in settings.local.json",
    "(gitignored); personal trust posture goes in ~/.claude/settings.json.",
    "",
    "NO defaultMode HERE, DELIBERATELY. Project settings override user settings, so a",
    "defaultMode pinned here would silently outrank ~/.claude/settings.json and impose",
    "one operator's autonomy level on every clone, collaborator and cloud runner. The",
    "repo carries the RULE SURFACE (allow/ask/deny) — reviewable, diffable, safe to",
    "share. The mode is the human's call, per machine.",
    "",
    "Precedence is deny > ask > allow. That is what lets the broad runner allows",
    "(uv:*, pnpm:*, docker:*) coexist with narrow gates on their dangerous",
    "subcommands. If a rule below looks redundant with a broader allow, it is not —",
    "it is the gate that outranks it.",
    "",
    "Gating rationale, tied to the repo's own standing rules:",
    "  - git push / gh mutations   → ADR-0005: integrate via PR, never push to main.",
    "  - alembic upgrade/revision  → migrations touch a live DB; CI's diff-guard",
    "                                already refuses to treat alembic/versions/** as",
    "                                generated, because migrations need real review.",
    "  - alembic downgrade         → denied outright: destructive schema rollback.",
    "  - .env* / secrets/ / env    → AGENTS.md: never read or write these. `env` and",
    "                                `printenv` are denied because they dump",
    "                                SIYUR_DATABASE_URL and the Google OIDC secrets",
    "                                straight into the transcript.",
    "  - lockfiles                 → AGENTS.md: fix the generator, never hand-edit",
    "                                generated output. uv.lock/pnpm-lock.yaml are",
    "                                resolver output.",
    "  - ~/code/siyur-course       → the course repo is observed one-way; this repo",
    "                                emits exhibit tags and issues, never edits it.",
    "  - this file + .claude/hooks → ask. Every gate above is advisory to an agent",
    "                                that can quietly widen its own rules first.",
    "",
    "PATH DENIES BIND THE READ TOOL, NOT BASH. `grep KEY .env` is a different code",
    "path from `Read(./.env)`, and the runner allows (uv:*, python3:*, grep:*) are far",
    "too broad to close that by pattern without flooding every session with prompts.",
    ".claude/hooks/guard_secrets.py inspects the Bash command string and is the layer",
    "that actually closes it. Defence in depth — the deny rules remain the real",
    "boundary — and it FAILS OPEN by design, because a hook that crashes on every",
    "tool call is worse than one that misses a case (FAIL-002). Covered by",
    "tests/test_agent_hooks.py.",
    "",
    "Run scripts/permission_report.py to see which calls are still prompting and what",
    "rule would cover them."
  ],
  "env": {
    "CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS": "1"
  },
